---
// src/components/Dek.astro — the one-line summary that sits under a section
// heading and says what the section is about before you read it.
//
// A newspaper dek: italic, muted, one rung under the heading and one above the
// prose. Its job is to make the contents list in the rail useful — you can
// jump to "Research", read one line, and know whether to stay.
//
// Keep it to a single line in the 800px main column (~65 characters at
// --text-lg). Two lines is a lede, and a lede belongs at the top of the page,
// not at the top of a section.
//
// A dek is the heading's second line, so the rule that closes a section header
// belongs under the PAIR — which means the dek draws it, and the h2 stands its
// own rule down whenever one of these follows it (see the `h2:has(+ .dek)`
// rule in pages/projects/[id].astro).
//
// Split into a box and a span for the same reason SectionHeading.astro is: the
// box draws the rule and box-snaps, the span inside takes the baseline
// transform. A border on a baseline-snapped element gets dragged off the grid.
// The tagger skips p.dek so it doesn't put data-snap back on the box.
---
<p class="dek" data-snap-box><span class="dek__text" data-snap><slot /></span></p>
